From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 12:12:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] fp8 : aiter-style wmma port: 128x64 CTA, 8 warps, 2
 CTAs/CU

Port the aiter gemm_a8w8_blockscale recipe into mul_mat_fp8_wmma:
- CTA 128 weight rows x 64 tokens (was 32 x 128), 8 warps, 2x2 wmma
  tiles per warp, grouped-M pid swizzle (GROUP_SIZE_M=4)
- single-buffered smem (26.4 KB) so 2 CTAs fit per CU (was 1 CTA at
  61 KB double-buffered): the occupancy jump 8->16 warps/CU is the
  real aiter win on gfx1201 (58 -> 77 TFLOP/s)
- register-staged k-block pipelining: loads for cb+1 issue before the
  wmma chain of cb, commit to smem between the two per-block barriers
- launcher: 1D swizzled grid, n_pad now ceil(n/64)*64 (matches the
  CTA span - fixes the 17<=n<=64 OOB staging read), dedicated block
  sizes for quantize (128) and GEMV (128)

Measured: pp512 4929.8 -> 5546-5596 t/s (+12.5-13.5%), tg64 unchanged.
All 1186 MUL_MAT backend-ops tests pass; generation matches the BF16
reference model.

Docs: AITER_FINDINGS.md (aiter inspection + results, incl. the LLVM
burst-array miscompile), HANDOVER.md, PERF_HANDOVER.md (next-session
perf tracking).

